# tool-output-slim: scripted agent turns exercising the slim tool I/O surfaces end-to-end.
# Lane: scratch cwd seeded with root mailbox (2 unread informational + 1 read), 3 agents
# (1 stopped with a dead letter), one 8-node task. Run:
#   pi --provider mock-llm --model tool-output-slim -e ./extensions/mock-llm -e ./extensions/swarm
# (from the seeded scratch cwd, with PI_SWARM_AGENT_ID=root PI_SWARM_IS_ROOT=1)
# NOTE: do NOT pass -e ./extensions/swarm on top of the repo's global packages entry —
# double registration aborts extension load. Either flag alone is enough.
# Transcript assertions: check_mailbox default scan is headers-only ≤2,050B with age/unread;
# fullBody:true returns complete bodies minus transport fields; agent_status default is the
# attention/census view (census+attention+hint, paneAlive/driver/target/slot); targeted query
# returns the full row; task_status default is the compact summary (progress/current/ready).
# Tester extension (swarm-tool-output-slim-20260928 / node test): turn 3 adds coverage for the
# two changed code paths the implementer's fixture did not reach end-to-end —
# (a) the §5 root-note trim on swarm_send_message (root recipient →
#     "(root: mailbox-only — durable in mailbox, no time-bound surface guarantee; normal)"), and
# (b) the worker unread ledger path (PI_SWARM_AGENT_ID=worker-01 scan with
#     pendingOnly:true + markDelivered:true → headers-only rows keyed off
#     st.delivered["worker-01"]; after marking, a second pendingOnly scan returns 0).
# Tester extension (swarm-tool-output-slim-20260928 / node test): turn 1 adds a
# pendingOnly+markDelivered scan (markDelivered path + ledger-keyed pendingOnly filter), turn 3 adds
# coverage for the two changed code paths the implementer's fixture did not reach end-to-end —
# (a) the §5 root-note trim on swarm_send_message (root recipient →
#     "(root: mailbox-only — durable in mailbox, no time-bound surface guarantee; normal)"), and
# (b) the worker unread ledger path — run a SECOND lane in the same scratch with
#     PI_SWARM_AGENT_ID=worker-01: the turn-1 scans key off st.delivered["worker-01"]
#     (worker side) instead of surfacedAt (root side), and the markDelivered scan durably
#     appends the returned ids to the worker ledger.
